{"name":"Pale Cherry Blossom","hex":"#fdeff2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Light in color.","Having a pallor (a light color, especially due to sickness, shock, fright etc.)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn pale; to lose colour.","To become insignificant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale"},{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"},{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry blossom","blocks":[{"text":"The cherry blossom, or sakura, is the flower of trees in Prunus subgenus Cerasus. Sakura usually refers to flowers of ornamental cherry trees, such as cultivars of Prunus serrulata, not trees grown for their fruit. Cherry blossoms have been described as having a vanilla-like smell, which is mainly attributed to coumarin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg/330px-Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","